      "src": "II:4",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "Sometimes, we try to subtract a mixed number… 3 4/10 - 1 7/10 We subtract the whole number…",
      "expected": "2 + 4/10 - 7/10",
      "demo": "*2 + 4/10 - 7/10*"
    },
    {
      "src": "II:12",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "Now, seven is greater than five, so we can’t subtract it without getting into negative values… 2 + (-3/10) ...which we’re not going to do just yet. Instead, we’re going to get to result a different way. When we see that the fist fraction is smaller than the second, we rewrite the first mixed number … 3 4/10 - 1 7/10 … like this:",
      "expected": "2 14/10 - 1 7/10",
      "demo": "*2 14/10 - 1 7/10*"
    },
    {
      "src": "II:16",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "In this case: 3 6/10 - 1 7/10 We would rewrite it like this:",
      "expected": "2 16/10 - 1 7/10",
      "demo": "*2 16/10 - 1 7/10*"
    },
    {
      "src": "II:20",
      "role": "model",
      "mode": "typed",
      "prompt": "And here… 24 6/10 - 1 7/10 We would rewrite it like this:",
      "expected": "23 16/10 - 1 7/10",
      "demo": "*23 16/10 - 1 7/10* Each time, we subtract one from the whole number, and add the bottom of the fraction to the top."
    },
